00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.670
When nuclear bombs obliterate the earth or
a virus wipes out the human race or robots

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:20.500
push mankind out of existence the US Government
believes that democracy should continue on.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.250
The country believes that, even if the population
of the US ceases to exist, the country should

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.250
go on.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:32.439
Akin to its almost paranoid nature, the US
government has a series of defined protocols

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:37.859
on how to continue the country when the country
is no longer—the Continuity of Government

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:38.859
Plans.

00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:43.260
You probably already know about part of these
plans because you probably know about the

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.329
US president’s line of succession.

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:50.409
If the president dies, there’s a list of
17 people ranging all the way from the Vice

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:55.469
President down to the Secretary of Homeland
Security who would take their place.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:01.190
With such a long list, the chances of the
US going without a president are near none.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.531
The one time a year when the entire line gathers
together—the state of the Union—one individual

00:01:06.531 --> 00:01:11.950
in the line of succession is appointed designated
survivor to wait out in a bunker to run the

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.329
government if the rest of it dies.

00:01:14.329 --> 00:01:18.320
But the line of succession is the basic stuff,
the stuff people already know.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.799
What’s far less known is the semi-secret
protocols and places that the government has

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:26.320
spent billions of dollars and decades building.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.299
However, until just 60 or 70 years ago the
US felt it was untouchable.

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:37.299
At no time in history had an enemy existed
as relatively close to the US as during the

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:38.520
cold war.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.549
The US’ foreign policy always kept in mind
that an ocean separated it from its enemies

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:48.109
but with the invention of nuclear bombs an
enemy could go from declaring war on the US

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:51.590
to toppling its government in a matter of
hours.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:56.869
During these days the US government began
actively preparing for doomsday.

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:01.710
There are four main bunkers from which the
US Government would run the country following

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:08.570
a world-ending event—the Presidential Emergency
Operations Center, Raven Rock Mountain Complex,

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:13.430
Mount Weather Emergency Operations Center,
and the Cheyenne Mountain Complex.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:18.550
The President is the most important person
to survive doomsday both for symbolic and

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.560
logistical reasons.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:25.650
If a nuclear warhead is inbound to Washington,
he or she would most likely evacuate downstairs

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.030
from the White House into their underground
bunker but that’s not guaranteed.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.620
During the Truman administration, the President
refused to leave the oval office during what

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.690
was believed to be an attack.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:41.030
This ended up being a false alarm, but some
presidents have said that they believe they

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:43.910
should ride out an attack with the rest of
the population.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:47.510
It’s just like saying “a captain should
go down with their ship.”

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.810
The Oval Office, and even the White House
Bunker is not the safest place someone can

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.520
be during an attack, but morale saves lives
and seeing a President braving out the fight

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.330
can help create a sense of national unity
that would keep the country together.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:07.030
A single person is replaceable, but the government
as a whole is more delicate.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.780
Raven Rock, Pennsylvania would serve as the
underground Pentagon.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.550
All the leaders of the armed forces will evacuate
by helicopter to this facility in the event

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.350
of an attack and command their troops across
the country and the world.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.780
During an attack of an apocalyptic scale,
it’s likely that Martial Law would be imposed

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.850
meaning that the military would take over
day-to-day control of the country.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.880
The commanders would have wide-ranging almost
dictatorial powers and habeas corpus would

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.000
be revoked.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.250
From distributing food, to serving as law
enforcement, to keeping the lights on, the

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:44.760
armed forces would truly work on the front
line of rebuilding a destroyed country.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.650
The Cheyenne Mountain Complex just out of
Colorado Springs, Colorado would serve as

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:53.790
the home to NORAD—the agency responsible
for controlling and tracking the skies above

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.110
the US and Canada.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:04:00.760
So, if the above ground world proved too dangerous
for the country’s leadership, these four

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:06.110
underground bunkers would serve as home to
the bare bones of the US government, but what

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.710
about the rest of it?

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:13.310
Nearly 4.5 million people are employed by
the US federal government and they all work

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.750
to keep it running.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.250
Where would the hundreds of government agencies
go?

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:23.840
Well, nobody knows exactly—at least publicly—but
we do know how they would relocate.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.570
You might have heard of the DEFCON system—it
makes frequent appearances in movies—but

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.020
few have heard of COGCON.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:35.840
COGCON is a readiness level system that directs
agencies how to prepare for an activation

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.500
of the government’s continuity of government
plans.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.230
At COGCON 4—the lowest level—every US
Government agency must be able to relocate

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:49.940
to an alternate facility and perform basic
functions within 12 hours—it’s an incredibly

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.480
ambitious plan.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.810
At COGCON 3 this number goes down to 8 hours
then at COGCON 2 is when things get real.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.340
At this level doomsday is imminent.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:04.770
Every agency has three sites for their continuity
plan—A, B, and C—and the agency would

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:11.090
split into three corresponding teams—A,
B, and C. The A team would relocate to a secure

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:17.110
facility near its normal headquarters—probably
bunkers under DC—the B team would relocate

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:21.750
near the Mount Weather Facility, and the C
team would relocate to another undisclosed

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:22.750
facility.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.100
Each team would be ready to take over operations
at a moment’s notice.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.710
The A team would continue operations for as
long as possible—either until they’re

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.640
dead or communications are cut off.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.520
Then the B team would seamlessly take over
operations.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.580
If the B team falls, the C team would serve
as the final chance for the survival of the

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.940
government agency.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.120
When the surface of the earth is unsurvivable,
there is one other place to go other than

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.290
underground—to the sky.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:56.410
The traditional Air Force One has redundancy
upon redundancy and dozens of classified defense

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.889
measures, but there’s a different plane
from which the President might command the

00:05:59.889 --> 00:06:04.750
country after doomsday—the Boeing E-4 Advanced
Airborne Command Post.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:09.270
It became increasingly clear to leadership
under the Carter Administration that the bunkers

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.460
would do little to protect against a direct
nuclear strike.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:17.150
In fact, they would just concentrate the very
individuals that the enemy would attack into

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.540
a few holes in mountains.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:24.680
Surviving a nuclear blast while seven miles
above earth, however, is far more conceivable.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:28.680
This plane is sometimes referred to as, “Air
Force One when it matters.”

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.270
Whenever the President travels, one of these
planes is stationed at most a couple hundred

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.480
miles away.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.730
From this plane, the President can command
the country indefinitely.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:44.610
It can be refueled mid-air by tanker so, barring
technical issues, it can remain flying for

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.940
as long as the food and water lasts.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:53.699
In a doomsday scenario, this plane could literally
stay airborne for weeks at a time to keep

00:06:53.699 --> 00:06:56.130
the country’s leadership safe.

00:06:56.130 --> 00:07:00.199
After armageddon, the United States’ goal
would be to rebuild the ailing country with

00:07:00.199 --> 00:07:05.169
however many survivors remained, but how would
the country continue as the same country when

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:07.340
most everyone was dead?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:12.120
Because of the line of succession, the President
could be an unknown unelected official with

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:17.390
a bare-bones government of just a few thousand
people so what’s to say to a survivor in

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:23.000
Texas or Oregon or Alaska that it’s still
the same country continuing on.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.370
Well, what binds America together is a common
culture and legacy.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:31.949
Art and historical artifacts are the physical
representations of this and their survival

00:07:31.949 --> 00:07:35.520
would pose a powerful message about the state
of the Union.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.820
On Doomsday resources would be scarce and
disjointed so officials have had to make decisions

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.460
about which items to save and which would
be left behind.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.310
For example, priority would be given to Leonardo
Di Vinci’s Ginevra de’ Benci over Rogier

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:53.290
van der Weyden’s Saint George and the Dragon
and the Declaration of Independence would

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.630
be saved before the Constitution.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:08:00.290
Ideally, though, all three of the nation’s
most important documents—the Declaration

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:05.070
of Independence, the Constitution, and the
Bill of Rights would be evacuated from Washington.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:09.580
Grouped together they would be called “Freedom
Documents Group I” and while some high level

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:14.290
officials would evacuate Washington by road,
these three documents would get their own

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:20.100
helicopter straight to Mount Weather to continue
the powerful legacy of the United States.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:25.290
Nobody knows exactly how or if the US Government
will survive doomsday—all we know are some

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.460
of the plans.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.780
Plans are just plans though and do not account
for the unknown.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:34.990
In the event that the United States is truly
threatened by nuclear war, pandemic, or any

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.649
another world ending event, who knows if the
population will even believe they are still

00:08:39.649 --> 00:08:41.339
in the United States.

00:08:41.339 --> 00:08:45.370
Little distinguishes one country from another
other than what people think and if people

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.569
believe they are part of the country of Alaska
or the Kingdom of California then for the

00:08:49.569 --> 00:08:50.709
most part they are.

00:08:50.709 --> 00:08:56.089
If the principles of separation of power,
judicial review, checks and balances, limited

00:08:56.089 --> 00:09:01.180
government, federalism, and popular sovereignty
live on past the end, the continuity of government

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.959
plans have succeeded even if the members of
government die.

00:09:04.959 --> 00:09:10.360
These plans are not about saving the president
or the secretary of defense or any one person—they’re

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:15.230
about making sure the structure of democratic
government continues on through thick and

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.589
thin.

